===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂weh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|wynd}}, {{m|enm|wind}}, from {{inh|en|ang|wind||wind}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*wind}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*windaz}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro||*h₂wéh₁n̥tos|wind}}, from earlier {{m|ine-pro|*h₂wéh₁n̥ts||wind}}, derived from the present participle of {{m|ine-pro|*h₂weh₁-||to blow}}.

{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|nl|wind}}, {{cog|de|Wind}}, {{cog|fy|wyn}}, {{cog|no|-}} and {{cog|sv|vind}}, {{cog|is|vindur}}, {{cog|la|ventus}}, {{cog|cy|gwynt}}, {{cog|sa|वात|tr=vā́ta}}, {{cog|ru|ве́тер}}, perhaps {{cog|sq|bundë||strong damp wind}}. {{doublet|en|athlete}}, {{m|en|vent}}, {{m|en|weather}} and {{m|en|nirvana}}.
{{col-bottom}}

